    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71922" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβρίκᾰλα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, τά, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the young</i> of
			animals, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				143
			</span></i> (lyr.) :—a form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄβρια</span></b> , τά, is cited from <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				48
			</span></i>) and <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i>(<i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				616
			</span></i>) by <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>NA</u>
				7.47
			</span></i>. (Perh. cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμβρος</span> (leg.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμβριον</span> ?): <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χοιρίδιον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i> slave's name <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀμβρίας</span>
			coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χοιροθύων</span> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				5(2).429
			</span></i>.)</div>
